,"large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877498"}},{"id":"7443","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6265","description":"Yep, they were intentionally cut.  The run out of the drop is visible in the left side of the photo.","caption":"trees in last drop","poi_name":"last drop","subject":"","author":"Dave Meyer","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7443","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/7443"}},{"id":"877497","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877790","description":"Mike finishing a fun slide on the WB of the Oswegatchie","caption":"Mike finishing the slide","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Jim Dobbins","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877497","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877497"}},{"id":"877496","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877789","description":"This drop has broken at least 2 backs.  If you run it the word is the line is to the left.","caption":"Be Careful","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Jim Dobbins","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877496","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877496"}},{"id":"7442","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6265","description":"We found these trees in the last big drop above the takeout.  They are hard to see from above.  The drop is immediately below 2 sets of powerlines crossing the river.  Once you enter the drop, there is no way to avoid the trees.  They were INTENTIONALLY cut into the river recently, see photo # 2.  Scout and carry on the right.","caption":"trees in the last drop","poi_name":"last drop","subject":"","author":"Dave Meyer","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/7442","large":"https://api.americanw